The left‐action weights now include a negative position term (‑1) and a stronger negative velocity term (‑3) with a small positive bias, encouraging left thrust when the car is far left or moving leftward. The right‐action weights use the opposite signs (+1 for position, +3 for velocity) with zero bias, so right thrust is favored when the car is to the right of the valley or moving rightward. The idle action receives a large negative bias (‑5) and zero state weights, effectively removing the idle action from competition. This linear classifier should generate stronger, direction‑aligned pushes and add a position‑dependent bias, helping the car build enough momentum to reach the goal faster than the previous best configuration.
